  "final_text": "I created the dashboard and the alert rule. The rule is enabled and its first run finished with status `ok`.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` data view uses `timestamp` as its time field. It contains web access log records with these main fields:\n- **Request:** `request`, `url`, `extension`, `referer`, `agent`\n- **Response:** `response` (the HTTP status code, stored as a string) and `bytes`\n- **Client:** `clientip`, `machine.os`, `machine.ram`\n- **Location:** `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`\n- **Other:** `host`, `tags`, `memory`, `hour_of_day`\n\nI only looked at the field list. I couldn't sample actual values because Kibana's Console proxy is turned off on this instance.\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-0bebcb03 Web logs overview\"** (id `ec09ca83-f1e3-4afe-a151-93809980d01e`). It has 8 panels and defaults to the time range now-7d to now+7d:\n- **Metric tiles:** total requests, unique visitors (distinct `clientip`), average bytes per request, total bytes\n- **Requests over time:** line chart\n- **Requests by response code:** bar chart\n- **Top 10 URLs:** horizontal bar chart\n- **Top 10 source countries:** bar chart\n\nI confirmed that all 8 panels were saved, but I haven't opened the dashboard in the browser to check that the charts display correctly.\n\n**3. Rule \"EFF-0bebcb03 5xx spike\"** (id `6ce4bc13-ed44-4b9a-98eb-687da0ab9da5`). This is an Elasticsearch query rule on the data view:\n- It runs every minute.\n- It counts documents matching `response.keyword : 5*` (any 5xx code).\n- It fires when that count is more than 10 within the last 5 minutes.\n\nThe rule has no actions attached, so when it fires it creates an alert in Kibana but doesn't send any notification. If you want emails or Slack messages, a connector needs to be added.",
